# Production build defaults (W0-2).
# VITE_* vars are bundled into the client and are PUBLIC by definition — never
# put secrets (API keys, tokens) here. This file only pins the API mode/base URL
# so a production build can never silently ship in mock mode.
#
# vite.config.ts fails the build (`npm run build`) if VITE_API_MODE !== "live"
# or VITE_API_BASE_URL is unset/points at localhost when mode=production, so a
# misconfigured or deleted value here breaks the build instead of shipping a
# prod bundle where login throws MockAuthDisabledError (src/lib/api.ts).

VITE_API_MODE=live

# Placeholder — replace with the real deployed influora-api URL before release.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.influora.com/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Money flags (F-0390)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read at src/lib/api.ts:71 and :104; `requirePaymentsEnabled` (api.ts:3014 topup, :3059
# withdraw, :3262 escrow-fund) and meera-api.ts:571 throw PaymentsUnavailableError BEFORE
# issuing the request when the matching flag is not the exact string "true".
#
# SCOPE — these two lines govern a LOCAL `npm run build` ONLY. They do NOT decide what the
# published ghcr.io/.../influora-web image does: Vite's loadEnv merges `process.env` over the
# .env files, the Dockerfile promotes every --build-arg to an ENV, and publish-images.yml always
# passes both flags explicitly — so the workflow's build-arg wins every time. Editing this file
# also matches no `paths:` filter in that workflow, so it triggers no rebuild. To change the
# SHIPPED behaviour, change .github/workflows/publish-images.yml (or the dispatch inputs).
#
# Until F-0390 these two were declared in NO build input at all — not here, not as a
# Dockerfile ARG, not in publish-images.yml — so Vite inlined nothing, both read false in
# every production bundle, and wallet top-up + escrow funding were dead with no lever to
# turn them on short of editing api.ts. Off-by-omission is not off-by-decision; these lines
# make the decision explicit and reviewable.
#
# Money IN — standard Razorpay (orders). ON per Swapnil's ruling on F-0390 (2026-08-25).
# Caveat recorded with that ruling: influora.razorpay.key-id is still REPLACE_ME in
# deploy/utho/generate-env.sh:59, so with the flag on, an unfunded environment now surfaces
# a server-side failure where it previously surfaced a clean "payments not enabled" notice.
# Provision RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET before pointing users at this build.
VITE_PAYMENTS_IN_ENABLED=true

# Money OUT — RazorpayX (payouts), a separately provisioned product. Stays OFF: this is the
# documented "collection live, payouts manual" operating state (api.ts:86-92), and
# WalletService.requestCreatorWithdrawal debits the creator's wallet BEFORE it calls
# RazorpayX — enabling this against an unconfigured gateway drops real creator balances and
# sends nothing, the orphaned-debit window PayoutOrphanedDebitSweepJob exists to sweep.
# Flip to true only once RAZORPAYX_ACCOUNT_NUMBER is genuinely provisioned.
VITE_PAYOUTS_ENABLED=false
